From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:26:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The brief-inventory API, round 3: the live-step API (the
 round-2 gate's finding 1)

- Configuration: the fields of `Action.apply` other than its work tapes (`simps`,
  `isSimp := false`): `Action.apply_state`, `_inputPos`, `_workTapePos`, `_output`. The work
  tapes keep `Simulation`'s `Action.apply_workTapes`.
- Deterministic: `MultiTapeTM.step_of_some` and `outputSymbol_of_some`, the live-state cases
  beside the upstream `step_of_halt` and `outputSymbol_of_halt`.
- Both vendoring headers list the additions (#116's precedent).

MIG-12's route (CfgRecord's window and observed-action helpers, and four more sites) and F5's
ruler host read these for an arbitrary action or machine. The review sub-agent's
`r3-repair.patch`, applied unchanged. Declarations only; no `@[simp]`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../TuringMachine/Configuration.lean          | 18 ++++++++++++-
 .../TuringMachine/Deterministic.lean          | 26 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

